        "description": "The workspace listing.\n\nAn envelope rather than a bare array, so that paging can arrive without\nbreaking every client — and so that a future `not_answered` has somewhere\nto live, which is the shape the capability probe already uses for the same\nreason (ADR-0058 decision 5).",
        "required": [
          "workspaces"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "workspaces": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/WorkspaceView"
            },
            "description": "Every workspace the caller may read, by slug. Archived ones included:\na listing that silently omitted them would make an archived workspace\nindistinguishable from one that never existed."
          }
        }
      },
      "WorkspaceView": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "A workspace, as the API serves it.\n\nA view rather than `synveda_types::workspace::Workspace` itself, because\nthis is the **contract** and the domain type is not: the two agree today\nand the day they need to differ — a computed field, a withheld one — the\ncontract must be able to say so without the storage type moving. `tenant_id`\nis deliberately absent: every `/v1` response is already scoped to the\ncaller's tenant, and echoing it invites a client to key on it.",
        "required": [
          "id",
          "scope_id",
          "slug",
          "display_name",
          "status",
          "revision",
          "created_at",
          "updated_at"
        ],
